  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Separate ownership",
      "items": [
        "Argo CD owns application objects after adoption; direct Helm refuses to overwrite an Argo-owned release.",
        "Terraform owns planned AWS foundations and the separate state-bootstrap root; it does not own application releases.",
        "The local runtime is kind, not EKS. AWS service topology is shown separately with official AWS icons."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Atlantis restrictions",
      "items": [
        "Historical isolated server smoke proves startup, health, readiness and metrics; GitHub webhook and PR-plan integration are pending.",
        "Only the exact aws-foundation project/directory is eligible. State bootstrap, unknown projects, traversal and mutating commands are denied.",
        "No AWS credentials, kubeconfig or Docker socket are supplied. No arrow to GitHub or AWS denotes an active integration."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Evidence and pending work",
      "items": [
        "G1 local runtime evidence is bound to f1603b3; G2-A offline gates to e3951d9. This source model does not relabel those checks.",
        "Jenkins has a real historical local pipeline result, separate agent and zero controller executors; Bitbucket remains an adapter.",
        "Foundation and enabled bootstrap graphs are mocked. The network-disabled real-provider bootstrap plan tested zero resources only."
      ]
    }
  ]
